module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleLocalGeneration.FromExtension
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartNonvanishingGeometricStalk
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartRestrictionFromSite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartRestrictionIntTensorPowers
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartRestrictionSections

/-!
# Reading a global section of a twist on a chart back as a section over the chart

Let `X` be an algebraic space over `S`, let `L` be an invertible `𝒪_X`-module, let `𝓕` be a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module and let `A` be an étale scheme chart of `X`.  Stacks 01Q3 (7), applied
on the scheme `chartScheme A` to the ample module `L|_A`, produces finitely many **global
sections** of

`(𝓕|_A) ⊗ (L|_A)^{⊗ n}`

generating that module — in this tree
`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isEventuallyGloballyGenerated_of_isAmple`, whose output is a
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` of the monoidal tensor product of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` with `Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule`.  The proof of
Stacks 0GUT reads those sections back as sections of `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ n}` over the étale chart `A`, so
that they may be enclosed in a finite-type submodule of the direct image on `Y`.  This file is
that reading.

Two steps are needed, and neither is a restatement of the other:

* the twist of the chart restriction has to be recognised as the chart restriction of the twist.
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorIntTensorPowIso` does this with both
  tensor products written in the `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor` spelling, whereas
  `Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule` and the global-generation statements use the monoidal structure
  `Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory` on the chart scheme.  The two are matched by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorIso`;
* a global section of the chart restriction has to be recognised as a section over the chart.
  This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.surjective_chartRestrictionTopSection`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorPowModuleIso`: the restriction to
  the chart of `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ k}` is the twist of the restriction of `𝓕` by the `k`-th power of
  `L|_A`, with the right-hand side in the monoidal spelling the global-generation statements use.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.surjective_chartTwistTopSection`: **every global section of
  `(𝓕|_A) ⊗ (L|_A)^{⊗ k}` is the image of a section of `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ k}` over the chart `A`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chartTwistSection`: the same as an existence statement.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chartTwistSections_of_generatingSections`: the family form,
  for a `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` of the twist on the chart — the shape Stacks 01Q3 (7)
  hands over.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_generatingSections_chartTwistSections_of_isAmple`:
  **Stacks 01Q3 (7) applied on the chart and read back on `X`**, assembled: for `L|_A` ample and
  `𝓕` quasi-coherent of finite type, every sufficiently positive twist of `𝓕|_A` is generated by
  finitely many global sections, each induced by a section of `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ n}` over the chart.

## Hypotheses carried, and why

`𝓕` is assumed quasi-coherent (`[F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite]`) and `L` invertible
(`[IsInvertibleModule X L]`).  Both are inputs rather than parts of the conclusion:

* quasi-coherence of `𝓕` is what makes the Zariski restriction to a chart monoidal — the
  restriction is a right adjoint, so only lax monoidal in general — and is already a hypothesis
  of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorIntTensorPowIso`.  In Stacks
  0GUT the module `𝓕` is quasi-coherent of finite type by hypothesis;
* invertibility of `L` is a hypothesis of Stacks 0D31, hence of Stacks 0GUT, and is what the
  integer tensor powers `L^{⊗ k}` of Stacks 01CU are defined from on either side.

No finiteness, affineness or separatedness hypothesis is used: the identification and the
read-back of sections are chartwise statements about one chart.

## Implementation notes

The monoidal structure on the modules of the chart scheme is introduced by
`attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory`, which is the
instance under which `Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule` and
`Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.IsEventuallyGloballyGenerated` are stated, so that no further
comparison of monoidal structures is needed on the chart side.

The read-back of a section is surjective but **not** injective in general, and nothing here
claims it is: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictionTopSection` is the sheafification unit of
the chart restriction followed by restriction along
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartOpensTopHom`, and only the first of those is known to be bijective
here.  Surjectivity is all the proof of Stacks 0GUT uses: it needs *some* section over the chart
inducing each generating global section.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GUT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GUT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory Opposite

universe u

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S) (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
  (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) [IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- **The restriction to an étale chart of a twist `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ k}`, with the chart side in the
monoidal spelling.**  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorIntTensorPowIso` composed with
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorIso`, which identifies the monoidal tensor product of
`Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory` with the `sheafTensor` spelling.

The monoidal spelling is the one `Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule` and the global-generation
statements of Stacks 01Q3 are written in. -/
def chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorPowModuleIso (A : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) [F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite] (k : ℤ) :
    chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u + 1, u, u, u, u}
          (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).obj F).obj (intTensorPowModule B S hS X L k)) A ≅
      chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A ⊗
        Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule (chartScheme A)
          (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X L A) k :=
  chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorIntTensorPowIso B S hS X L A F k ≪≫
    (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorIso (chartScheme A).presheaf
      (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf (chartScheme A))
      (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A)
      (Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule (chartScheme A)
        (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X L A) k)).symm

/-- The global section of `(𝓕|_A) ⊗ (L|_A)^{⊗ k}` induced by a section of `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ k}` over the
étale chart `A`: the chart restriction of the section, read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorPowModuleIso`. -/
def chartTwistTopSection (A : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    [F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite] (k : ℤ)
    (s : (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u + 1, u, u, u, u}
      (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).obj F).obj (intTensorPowModule B S hS X L k)).val.obj
        (op A)) :
    Γ(chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A ⊗
      Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule (chartScheme A)
        (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X L A) k, ⊤) :=
  (chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorPowModuleIso B S hS X L A F k).hom.app ⊤
    (chartRestrictionTopSection B S hS X _ A s)

/-- **Every global section of the twist `(𝓕|_A) ⊗ (L|_A)^{⊗ k}` on the chart's scheme comes from
a section of `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ k}` over the étale chart `A`.**

The comparison of the two readings of the twist is an isomorphism, so bijective on sections over
`⊤`, and every global section of a chart restriction comes from a section over the chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.surjective_chartRestrictionTopSection`). -/
theorem surjective_chartTwistTopSection (A : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) [F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite] (k : ℤ) :
    Function.Surjective (chartTwistTopSection B S hS X L A F k) := by
  have hiso : Function.Surjective
      ((chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorPowModuleIso B S hS X L A F k).hom.app ⊤) :=
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
      ((chartRestrictionSchemeModuleTensorPowModuleIso B S hS X L A F k).hom.app ⊤)).2
  exact hiso.comp (surjective_chartRestrictionTopSection B S hS X _ A)

/-- The existence form of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.surjective_chartTwistTopSection`. -/
theorem exists_chartTwistSection (A : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) [F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite] (k : ℤ)
    (t : Γ(chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A ⊗
      Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule (chartScheme A)
        (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X L A) k, ⊤)) :
    ∃ s : (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u + 1, u, u, u, u}
      (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).obj F).obj (intTensorPowModule B S hS X L k)).val.obj
        (op A),
      chartTwistTopSection B S hS X L A F k s = t :=
  surjective_chartTwistTopSection B S hS X L A F k t

/-- **The family form: a generating family of global sections of the twist on the chart, read
back as sections over the chart.**  For `σ` a family of global sections of
`(𝓕|_A) ⊗ (L|_A)^{⊗ k}` generating it, there is a family of sections of `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ k}` over the
étale chart `A`, indexed by the same type, inducing the members of `σ`.

This is the shape in which Stacks 01Q3 (7) — here
`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isEventuallyGloballyGenerated_of_isAmple` — hands its output to the
proof of Stacks 0GUT; the index type is unchanged, so its finiteness is carried along. -/
theorem exists_chartTwistSections_of_generatingSections (A : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) [F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite] (k : ℤ)
    (σ : (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A ⊗
      Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule (chartScheme A)
        (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X L A) k).GeneratingSections) :
    ∃ s : σ.I → (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u + 1, u, u, u, u}
      (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).obj F).obj (intTensorPowModule B S hS X L k)).val.obj
        (op A),
      ∀ i, chartTwistTopSection B S hS X L A F k (s i) = (σ.s i).eval (op ⊤) :=
  let ⟨g, hg⟩ := (surjective_chartTwistTopSection B S hS X L A F k).hasRightInverse
  ⟨fun i => g ((σ.s i).eval (op ⊤)), fun _ => hg _⟩

/-- **Stacks 01Q3 (7) applied on an étale chart, with its output read back on `X`.**  Let `L` be
an invertible `𝒪_X`-module whose restriction to the scheme of an étale chart `A` is ample, and
let `𝓕` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type on the small étale site.  Then there is
an `n₀` such that for every `n ≥ n₀` the twist `(𝓕|_A) ⊗ (L|_A)^{⊗ n}` is generated by finitely
many global sections, each of which is induced by a section of `𝓕 ⊗ L^{⊗ n}` over the chart `A`.

This is `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isEventuallyGloballyGenerated_of_isAmple` on the chart
scheme — its two hypotheses being supplied by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherent_restrictToChart` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteType_restrictToChart` — followed by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chartTwistSections_of_generatingSections`.

Ampleness of `L|_A` is taken as a hypothesis rather than derived: it is what relative ampleness
of `L` supplies on a chart lying over an affine chart of the target, through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAmple_chartRestrictionSchemeModule_of_isRelativelyAmple`, and the
chart has to come from such a square for it to hold at all. -/
theorem exists_generatingSections_chartTwistSections_of_isAmple (A : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hamp : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple (chartScheme A) (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X L A))
    (F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) [hFqc : F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite]
    (hFft : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite F) :
    ∃ n₀ : ℤ, ∀ n : ℤ, n₀ ≤ n →
      ∃ σ : (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A ⊗
          Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule (chartScheme A)
            (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X L A) n).GeneratingSections,
        Finite σ.I ∧
          ∃ s : σ.I → (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u + 1, u, u, u, u}
            (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).obj F).obj
              (intTensorPowModule B S hS X L n)).val.obj (op A),
            ∀ i, chartTwistTopSection B S hS X L A F n (s i) = (σ.s i).eval (op ⊤) := by
  have hqc : (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A).IsQuasicoherent :=
    isQuasicoherent_restrictToChart B S hS X F hFqc A
  have hft : (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_restrictToChart B S hS X F hFqc hFft A
  obtain ⟨n₀, hn₀⟩ := Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isEventuallyGloballyGenerated_of_isAmple
    (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X L A) hamp
    (chartRestrictionSchemeModule B S hS X F A) hqc hft
  refine ⟨n₀, fun n hn => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := hn₀ n hn
  exact ⟨σ, hσ, exists_chartTwistSections_of_generatingSections B S hS X L A F n σ⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
